{% decision_card number="ADR-0004" status="superseded" %}
One decision. Status reviewed 2026-07-27.
{% /decision_card %}

## Context

Claude and Codex sessions can end or hit capacity, so repository memory must outlive either tool.

## Decision drivers

- Cross-provider continuity
- Lower repeated context
- Deterministic verification

## Options considered

- Chat-only memory
- File handoff only
- Immediate autonomous broker

## Decision

Originally adopted a file-only handoff and deferred a broker during Phase 1.

## Positive consequences

- Established repository-first memory
- Reduced transcript transfer

## Negative consequences

- No typed routing or context package

## Risks

- The no-broker clause became inconsistent with the later explicit execution mandate

## Follow-up work

- Retain compact handoffs
- Use ADR-0007 for the approved in-repository simulation boundary

## Supersedes or superseded by

Superseded in part by ADR-0007. Repository-first memory remains valid.

